Code submitted to this repo should adhere to the following rules:
  - Code cannot have been generated fully or in-part by an LLM or other form of AI.
  - Contributor must explicitly state in their contribution request that they did not use AI in the contributed content.
  - Code-style must closely conform to that of surrounding code in the repo. This is not strictly required, it will just be fixed afterwards.

Before submitting new code, you are expected to have rebuilt, used, then tested the project to make sure you have not introduced new issues or broken anything.
New code that cannot be compiled or fails automated tests will be rejected until fixed or will be reimplemented by a maintainer.
